        }
      ],
      "message": "wallet: avoid int overflow in listtransactions\n\nlisttransactions adds the count and skip arguments as int. Both are\nchecked to be non-negative, but their sum can still exceed INT_MAX.\nFor example `listtransactions \"*\" 2147483647 1` overflows, the loop\nstops after the first entry, and the clamp afterwards overflows the\nsame way. push_backV is then called with an iterator range far outside\nthe vector, which crashes the node.\n\nDo the additions in int64_t. Add a functional test with count + skip\nabove INT_MAX.",
